# Allow the unprivileged PhotoStructure runtime user to invoke the
# consent-gated codec installer helper without a password prompt. The
# helper itself is root-owned, 0755, and accepts no arguments — the
# trailing `""` is a sudoers pattern meaning "no args allowed".
#
# Why two rules: docker-entrypoint.sh creates a `photostructure` user
# with `useradd --non-unique --uid $PUID`. When PUID=1000 (default), the
# UID collides with the base image's pre-existing `node` user. Per
# sudoers(5), "two users with the same user-ID are considered distinct"
# — getpwuid(1000) returns whichever is first in /etc/passwd (`node`),
# so a rule for the `photostructure` *name* never matches. The `#1000`
# UID-match rule covers that case; the `photostructure` name-match rule
# covers custom PUID (which gets a unique UID, no collision).
#
# Sudoers UID syntax: `#NNN` in a user-list position is parsed as UID
# NNN, not a comment. See sudo.ws/docs/man/*/sudoers.man/.
photostructure ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /opt/photostructure/bin/install-codec-tools.sh ""
#1000 ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /opt/photostructure/bin/install-codec-tools.sh ""
